# Docker

The `robot-gateway`, `capture-pipeline`, and `webrtc-client-go` images exist. Root Compose starts `capture`, `gateway`, and `webrtc` (`compose.yaml` + `deploy/compose.dev.yaml` or `deploy/compose.robot.yaml`). Remaining ROS images wait.

- One Dockerfile per service. ROS images use an explicit `ros:jazzy-*` tag.
- A Go image uses a multi-stage build and a minimal runtime base.
- `capture-pipeline` uses Debian 13, not `ros:jazzy-*`. It has no ROS 2.
- Any build context that copies source has a `.dockerignore`.
- `privileged: true` needs an ADR that names the device it unlocks. Capture on Pi 5: ADR 0009, OV5647 / libcamera.
- `network_mode: host` does not by itself share Cyclone DDS memory between containers. Check the Cyclone configuration before relying on shared memory.
- The robot runs pinned images. It does not rebuild on every start.
